    array becomes one small IMMUTABLE SQL helper,
    public.text_array_entries_all_populated(text[]): at least one entry, no NULL entry, no blank
    or whitespace-only entry. It references only pg_catalog names, so it is safe under
    `search_path = ''`, and its EXECUTE is revoked from PUBLIC like every other function here.
    cardinality(ARRAY[NULL]) is 1, which is why counting slots was never enough.
  * The function body's volunteer branch mirrors both, so a direct caller still gets a stated
    reason rather than a bare constraint name: the handle and summary are trimmed with an
    EXPLICIT whitespace set, and the languages get a second, distinct refusal for a null or blank
    entry. The trim set spells the vertical tab in octal because PostgreSQL escape strings have
    no \v - E'\v' is the letter v, which would have stripped every v out of handles.

R4 (the RPC signature replacement had no compatibility bridge). Source co-location is not
deployment atomicity, and the migration comment said otherwise.
  * The four new parameters get `default null`, so a call carrying only the original five named
    arguments still resolves. There is still exactly one function, so the drop-first reasoning is
    untouched - a default is not an overload.
  * complete-signup/index.ts now OMITS the four github keys from the rpc body when the judged
    handle is null, rather than sending them as nulls. An NGO completion therefore travels as the
    original five keys and works against either schema version. Sending explicit nulls would name
    arguments an older function does not have and fail to resolve.
  * The drop paragraph and the plan's risk 2 now state the honest residual: during a mixed-plane
    window volunteer completion is unavailable, fail-closed under migration-first.

R5 (the no-table-grants claim contradicted the committed capture). Supabase ships default
privileges for the public schema, so the new table arrived already carrying REFERENCES, TRIGGER
and TRUNCATE for all three Data API roles - the absence of a grant statement is not the absence
of a privilege. The migration gains
`revoke all on table public.volunteer_profiles from anon, authenticated, service_role`, and the
comment now states the measured reality instead of inferring it.

R3 (no test executed extractGithubHandle). The fixture's completeSignup now renders its stored
state as the canonical GoTrue /auth/v1/user shape and derives the caller fact through the SHIPPED
extractor, exactly as resolveCaller does. Storage stays storage; test bodies are unchanged.

Step 3's done-criterion re-run: `bun run db:reset` replays clean, and migration-replay.txt is
refreshed with the helper's pg_proc row and ACL, the new constraint definitions, the four DEFAULT
NULL parameters as the catalog reports them, and the table-privilege matrix for all five public
tables. volunteer_profiles shows ZERO rows for the three roles; the other four tables carry the
same pre-existing residue and are measured, not fixed, per ruling R5's scope note.

`bun run typecheck` green.

