COMMIT:766fcbd489da97ba2193a47f6f05e19a5a857d66
SUBJECT:AI4DEV-58: step 5 - the three GitHub acceptance tests, written; the two existing ones amended
BODY:AT-001.02, .04 and .05 stop being declared stubs and get real bodies. All
seven ids in the signup-and-sign-in file are now written, which completes the
first deliverable of the authentication requirement at loop tier.

AT-001.02 drives all three clauses: a github-established session completes as
a volunteer, the account carries the handle that signed up, and a later
provider sign-in resolves to the SAME account rather than minting a second.

AT-001.04 drives BOTH establishing providers the criterion names - email and
Google - because the gate reads a linked identity and a gate accidentally
written against the session provider would only show up if both were run. Each
refusal must name GitHub and linking, and must leave no account row, no
profile, no acknowledgment and no platform acknowledgment behind. Then the
byte-identical request succeeds once the identity is linked, so the link is
provably the cause. An NGO control completes with no GitHub identity at all,
which is what pins the gate's shape rather than merely its existence.

AT-001.05 asserts the pre-completion negative first: after linking and BEFORE
completion the profile is null. Without it, an implementation that populated
at link time or queued an empty row would satisfy everything after the
completion, and the causal claim would be untested. Then the profile is read
immediately after completion returns - handle by value, languages non-empty
AND equal to the declared import source's output, a non-negative whole
repository count, a non-blank summary. The test says in its own comment that
the source is a stub, so no green here can be read as a real import.

The two existing green tests each gain one linkGithubIdentity call as a
PRECONDITION - the gate makes their old volunteer setup impossible - and not
one assertion of theirs changes. The load-bearing comment about the shipped
path never receiving a provider is RETAINED: only its stale mechanical clause
is updated, plus one sentence stating that a linked-GitHub fact is not the
session provider and the equivalence claim stays exactly as narrow.

Surface marks per the plan: .02 and .04 join .01, .03 and .07 as ui, so the
wiring leaf re-runs them; .05 stays backend because its observable is row
contents. The expected file flips the three ids to green - 7 green, 30 red -
the D1.L2 leaf label is removed from the pending map now that nothing points
at it, and pending-ledger.txt names all 30 remaining ids against the manifest.

bun run typecheck exits 0. THE VERIFY SUITE IS DELIBERATELY NOT RUN in this
sitting: this is a draft, meant to be critiqued as real code before it is
polished green.

