SUBJECT:AI4DEV-58: step 4 - the edge function carries the caller fact, and GitHub is configured
BODY:resolveCaller now answers with the caller's id AND the handle of any linked
GitHub identity, extracted by the shared pure module from the same
/auth/v1/user response it already fetched - the one-line extension the old
comment reserved for the leaf that needed it. The establishing provider is
still deliberately not carried: a linked identity is a different fact, and
nothing shipped branches on email-vs-Google.

complete-signup passes that fact into validateCompleteSignup as its second
argument - never a request field - and, when the judged value carries a
handle, computes the stub import stats for it and sends handle and stats into
the same rpc call as the account. One round trip, one transaction, no queue.

config.toml: enable_manual_linking flips to true, because GoTrue refuses
linkIdentity outright while it is false and that link is what the criterion
about completing volunteer signup describes. A new auth.external.github block
mirrors the google one, with no skip_nonce_check - a nonce is an OpenID
Connect accommodation and GitHub is plain OAuth2, so there is nothing to skip.

Measured after a full stack restart, recorded in step4-serves.txt: the
preflight is answered 204 with our own CORS header set, an unauthenticated
POST is refused 401 with our own sentence (so the module carrying the new
import really loaded inside the Deno runtime), create-organization still
serves, and /auth/v1/settings reports github true. No GitHub OAuth credential
is set, which is the expected case and blocks nothing. Exercising a signup end
to end belongs to the later proof sitting and is not claimed here.

