COMMIT:4be143d1977c3a5427c1a13aabcdb362e40cb4cb
SUBJECT:AI4DEV-58: step 3 - volunteer_profiles, and complete_signup dropped and recreated with the gate
BODY:One new migration. public.volunteer_profiles holds the onboarding import keyed
by the account, with four CHECK constraints that make the criterion's clause
about a queued-but-empty import a shape rather than a convention.

The languages constraint is cardinality(top_languages) >= 1 and NOT
array_length(...) >= 1: array_length returns NULL for an empty array, and a
CHECK whose expression is NULL passes, so the array_length form would have
enforced nothing on the one input it exists to refuse. The catalog capture
shows that fact evaluated by this PostgreSQL.

complete_signup is dropped and recreated with four added parameters rather
than created alongside the old one, because an overload makes PostgREST refuse
the rpc name as ambiguous. Every previous refusal is reproduced word for word.
New: a volunteer completion needs all four import parameters non-empty, and
needs a row in auth.identities with provider github AND identity_data
user_name equal to the handle it claims - existence alone would let a
service-role caller commit a profile under a handle the account never linked.
An NGO completion must carry none of the four.

Replayed from empty: bun run db:reset exits 0. The catalog confirms exactly one
pg_proc row named complete_signup, row-level security on with no policies, no
table privilege granted to any Data API role, and execute revoked from public
and granted only to service_role.

