8: 
9:     AtPending: <id> PENDING [sut-missing] -
10: 
11: and compares it from position 0. Everything AFTER the em dash is free. So a stub whose detail
12: read "todo" would satisfy `at:check`, `at:verify --expect` and CI alike, while the record said
13: nothing about who lands the id or when.
14: 
15: Nothing mechanical closes that. This file is the check that does: one line per pending id, and
16: every deliverable-and-leaf named below really appears in `loop/decomp/req-001.md` at revision
17: 0579425. A reviewer compares the two files. No per-stub oracle is built - that is harness work
18: and belongs to the harness item, not to a leaf.
