37: Rejected, on three grounds.
38: 
39: 1. **The state the reviewer describes violates nothing AT-001.05 says.** Its Given is *"a
40:    volunteer signup where GitHub is linked"* and its Then requires the handle and stats
41:    *"observably populated on the profile"*. When a link succeeds in Auth and the completion
42:    request never arrives, **no account row, no profile surface and no acknowledgment exist at
43:    all** â€” there is no profile to be unpopulated. That is an unfinished signup, not a completed
44:    link whose import went missing. "Queued-but-empty" names an import deferred after an account
45:    exists; the plan's design has no queue and no account until completion, so the forbidden state
46:    is unrepresentable â€” which is stronger than testable. AT-001.04's own text closes the loop:
47:    *"linking completes signup"* â€” within the signup flow the two moments the reviewer separates
48:    are the same moment.
49: 2. **The proposed firing point cannot be executed by any code this repository ships.** The link
50:    happens inside Supabase Auth's OAuth round trip; no webhook, hook or event reaches server
51:    code (D-C states this, and the reviewer names no mechanism). The plan gate's own contract
52:    makes "anything no tool can actually do" its target failure â€” firing at the link event is
53:    exactly that, short of a poller or a queue, and a queue manufactures the exact state the
54:    criterion forbids.
55: 3. **The wiring-leaf half of the claim is inverted.** AT-001.02 and AT-001.04 are marked `ui`
56:    and re-run `--wired`; the screen flow .04 drives is precisely link â†’ completion, and
57:    completion is the importer â€” so the "missing transition" is the very thing the wired re-run
58:    exercises. AT-001.05's observable is row contents, provider- and screen-independent, the same
59:    reasoning that left .06 backend.
